  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs`: the heavy-lane test `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_both_operations` becomes `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish`. It generates the 3D Finish S1 alone and verifies that no gate problem is a gouge.\n- A new default-suite test `the_sample_as_imported_refuses_the_3d_pocket_by_name` pins the 3D Pocket R1 refusal by its text (about 0.1 s).\n- `docs/decisions/1706-as-imported-pocket-refusal.md` records the decision.\n- No product code changes. No golden or snapshot changes.\n\n## The cause\n\nNo merge caused the failure. The test failed from its first commit.\n\n- The test came in commit `6726c1b81` (PR #1419). That commit and its merge `25df19ded` refuse in the same way.\n- A `git bisect --first-parent` from `25df19ded` to `origin/main` (`101d82f9d`) refuses at all seven merges that it ran.\n- The test is `#[ignore]`d, so the v0.20.0 release gate was its first run.\n- The sample imports with no notes and as three `Outward` bodies. The importer PRs #1671, #1576 and #1638 do not change it.\n\n## Why the refusal is correct\n\nA 3D Pocket's machine area is the model's own XY silhouette (`operation::material_source`, the `Pocket3D` arm). Each level erodes the area outside the part's section by the cutter radius (`machining3d::ladder`). The sample as imported casts a strip only 6.53 mm wide (Y -4.94 .. 1.59). No 6 mm end mill fits in it at any level. The ladder refuses with `nothing to cut: the model fills the pocket at every level`. Nothing cuts and nothing posts. A 70 x 12 x 120 mm box stock gives the same refusal, so the stock is not the cause. No law is weakened.\n\nThe message text names the wrong reason (\"the model fills\" where the area is narrower than the tool). Issue #1709 (`P7`) is the follow-up for the text.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test shared_face_bodies` (debug): the default tests pass, the heavy test is ignored.\n- `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test shared_face_bodies -- --include-ignored`: the default tests pass; the heavy 3D Finish test was still running after 12 min at push time. A later PR comment gives its result.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test shared_face_bodies -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full release gate and the other app suites.\n- The heavy test in debug (about 15 min or more).\n- The Windows-only and per-OS pinned readings of other suites.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1706\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
